data.content:
In .NET 10, `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded from **OpenAPI.NET v1 to v2**. This is a major breaking change affecting the object model. Here's what changed and how to fix each piece:

---

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` removed

OpenAPI.NET v2 uses native `JsonNode` instead of `IOpenApiAny`.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

Remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;` — the namespace no longer exists.

---

## 2. `OpenApiResponse` → response model changes

`operation.Responses` is now a `Dictionary<string, OpenApiResponse>` (not a custom collection with `TryAdd` semantics that auto-wraps). The fix is minor:

```csharp
// Before
operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

// After (same API, but ensure you're using the correct type)
operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });
```

This likely still compiles. If not, use:
```csharp
operation.Responses["401"] ??= new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" };
```

---

## 3. `OpenApiReference.Type` → `OpenApiReference.Id` only

References no longer use `ReferenceType`. The `Type` is inferred from context.

```csharp
// Before
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// After
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Id = "oauth2" }
};
```

If `Type` is still required in your version, use `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models` (the enum moved but may still exist).

---

## 4. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI v3.1 (which v2 of the library targets) replaced `nullable: true` with a type array. Use the `Type` flags:

```csharp
// Before
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10 / OpenAPI.NET v2)
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;  // remove null from type union

// To make nullable:
property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

Add `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;` (for `JsonSchemaType`).

---

## 5. `schema.Required` is now `ISet<string>` → `HashSet<string>`

This likely still works, but if you get errors:

```csharp
// Still valid
schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key)
```

---

## Full fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of breaking changes:**
| Concept | .NET 9 (OpenAPI.NET v1) | .NET 10 (OpenAPI.NET v2) |
|---------|------------------------|--------------------------|
| Dynamic values | `IOpenApiAny` / `OpenApiString` | `JsonNode` / `JsonValue` |
| Nullable | `schema.Nullable` | `schema.Type` flag with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| References | `ReferenceType` + `Id` | `Id` only (type inferred) |
